; A declarator binding `open`, the kernel's word of what a state owes and of
; its hypotheses, written directly: the **control** of the four routes,
; refused at the parse, where no declarator takes it.
;
; It is also the *module* the three import fixtures beside it pull in —
; `reserved_open_symbols`, `reserved_open_qualified`, `reserved_open_aliased`
; — so the four files are one declaration reached four ways. An import gives
; a module's names their full names, and a reserved name keeps its own: the
; import resolver reads the one reserved list, `ein_core::RESERVED`, so no
; route can carry a macro named `reserved_open_direct.open` past the loader.
;
; Every route is refused at this file's line 16.
;
(relation p T)

(macro open (?x) (p ?x))
